# .gitattributes
#
# Marks documentation as linguist-documentation so GitHub's language
# detection isn't dominated by the sheer volume of Markdown/prose in this
# repo (governance docs, ADRs, playbooks, BUILD_LOG.md, ROADMAP.md,
# handbook.txt) relative to the actual Python/Ansible/TypeScript that does
# the work. Python (attack/, detections/, config/inventory/, scripts/,
# platform/backend/) is the layer that's genuinely tested this build —
# the repo's language stats should reflect that.

*.md linguist-documentation
docs/** linguist-documentation
BUILD_LOG.md linguist-documentation
ROADMAP.md linguist-documentation
handbook.txt linguist-documentation
